-- **Legacy media and widget fidelity:** a legacy import now rewrites legacy storage URLs in imported message text, article bodies, the workspace logo, the widget background and teammate and assistant avatars to native URLs that serve the same bytes under native access rules: a conversation's file through its conversation, a logo, avatar or background to anyone (so the widget shows it on the customer's site), an article image to whoever may read an article that holds it. A URL whose file the package does not carry is left as written and counted (`mediaUrls` in the summary). The imported widget keeps legacy's look and behaviour: legacy's default colours under the saved overrides (the dashboard colour no longer recolours the launcher or send button), the schedule's days as numbers the dashboard reads and saves, no presence-based away, and the workspace shown as the team to an unassigned visitor; legacy keys the native widget does not read are listed (`widgetNotReproduced`). Apply `321_legacy_import_files.sql` after 320, then run `node scripts/legacy-import/upgrade.mjs --project <id>` once per workspace imported before this change. Documented in docs/LEGACY-EXPORT.md.
-- **Fixes — Cloudflare Email Sending account binding:** the deploy declaration (`deploy.json`, and `management/integration/managed-deploy.json` generated from it) now binds `EMAIL_ACCOUNT_ID`, the name the Worker reads, as an optional secret beside `MAIL_ACCOUNT_ID`, so a normal deploy can enable Cloudflare Email Sending. Before, a deploy sent only `MAIL_ACCOUNT_ID` and never delivered `EMAIL_ACCOUNT_ID` to the Worker: an installation of v0.4.12 to v0.4.17 that set `EMAIL_PROVIDER=cloudflare` got outbound mail unavailable, so sign-in links could not be sent. The binding is optional, so installations on Resend or SendGrid, or without mail, are unaffected. `scripts/delivery/secret-declarations.mjs`, run by `verify:build`, now also fails when an `EMAIL_*` name the Worker reads is not bound in the declaration. Existing installations keep their bindings; set `EMAIL_ACCOUNT_ID` privately and redeploy to enable Cloudflare mail. No migration.
-- **Fixes — setup and email-link sign-in during a knowledge upgrade:** an upgraded installation with imported history no longer answers `503` on `/api/identity/setup`, `/api/identity/setup-status`, `/api/identity/auth-options`, `/api/identity/sign-in-options`, `POST /api/identity/magic-link` and `POST /api/identity/magic-link/consume` while a workspace's knowledge conversion is unfinished (days on an installation with millions of imported rows). Those routes read no knowledge data, so password-less imported owners can request and use an emailed sign-in link at once, as password login and an existing session already could. The fence is otherwise unchanged: public knowledge pages and every other anonymous `/api/*` route (the customer widget, the portal, the public articles API) still answer `503` until every workspace's conversion finishes, and so do `forgot-password`, `link-status`, `accept-token`, `register` and `verify-email`. Member sessions are unaffected. No migration.
-- **Migrations:** `321_legacy_import_files.sql`. Apply once after `320_legacy_import_work_repair.sql` and before serving the updated Worker; it is additive and creates one empty table.
